   "en": "Crowded and increasingly well-capitalized field. Direct depth-camera competitors: Orbbec (China, now the de-facto RealSense successor, well-funded, public in China), Intel RealSense (winding down hardware but legacy installed base + spinout), Luxonis (OAK), StereoLabs (ZED), Zivid (high-end structured light), and Photoneo (acquired by Zebra Technologies in late 2024 — signals consolidation and strategic interest). In the application/solution layer (bin-picking, VGR), Mech-Mind (China, very well-funded), Photoneo/Zebra, and in-house perception teams at robot OEMs compete. NVIDIA itself both enables (Isaac) and commoditizes camera vendors. LIPS's differentiation is industrial ruggedization (IP67/M12), Isaac certification, multi-modality (ToF + stereo + structured light) and Taiwan supply-chain cost/manufacturing access — but it is a mid-tier player against larger Chinese (Orbbec, Mech-Mind) and Western (Zivid, Zebra/Photoneo) competitors."
