    "zh": "看多論點：紙面上是教科書般的 AppWorks 型標的——GSEA 在地的 AI B2B SaaS，乘著真實的法規順風（馬來西亞 2025 年 7 月的 BIM 強制規定）、一支可信的前 PETRONAS 技術團隊，以及一個西方既有業者忽視的在地化切入點（東南亞建築法規）。若 Rosary 全力投入 AEC-東南亞，該強制規定可能將其帶入橫跨 ASEAN 的經常性營收，而此階段一張 AppWorks 種子支票（US$200K–$2M 區間）正是 AppWorks 的進場點。加速器（AW#32，不收股權）讓 AppWorks 得以近距離、專屬地進行盡職調查。看空論點：這是一支尚未有營收、未獲資助、規模偏小的團隊，已轉型過一次（V-Cred→垂直 AI），如今又分散於四個垂直領域；「AEC 合規」可能只是定位，而非承諾。沒有可查證的進展、護城河薄弱／易被商品化、近期 SAM 規模有限，且 AEC 領域專業僅屬後天習得。AppWorks Funds 只對少數校友開出後續支票，並對進展＋可防守性＋專注度進行嚴格篩選——這三項目前皆弱。結論：今日不太可能成為後續支票標的。屬於觀察名單，而非下注。未來開支票的關鍵門檻問題：團隊是否會選定 AEC，並憑藉馬來西亞強制規定證明出付費、留存的客戶（將 Petronas／TNBR／CLJ 從標誌轉化為營收），以及他們能否展現在地化的領先優勢可複利累積成真正的護城河？透過加速器取得的強力創辦人接觸管道，使其值得持續追蹤至首輪定價募資，但在此階段尚未達到後續投資的門檻。",
    "en": "BULL CASE: Textbook AppWorks-shaped on paper — GSEA-native AI B2B SaaS, ridden by a genuine regulatory tailwind (Malaysia's July-2025 BIM mandate), a credible ex-PETRONAS technical team, and a localization wedge (SEA building codes) Western incumbents ignore. If Rosary commits to AEC-SEA, the mandate could pull them into recurring revenue across ASEAN, and an AppWorks seed check (US$200K-$2M range) at this stage is exactly AppWorks' entry point. The accelerator (AW#32, equity-free) gives AppWorks proprietary, close-range diligence access. BEAR CASE: This is a pre-revenue, unfunded, sub-scale team that has already pivoted once (V-Cred→vertical AI) and is now spread across four verticals; 'AEC compliance' may be positioning, not commitment. No verifiable traction, a thin/commoditizable moat, modest near-term SAM, and only-acquired AEC domain expertise. AppWorks Funds writes follow-on checks into a MINORITY of alumni and is discriminating on traction + defensibility + focus — all three are currently weak. VERDICT: Unlikely to be a follow-on check TODAY. Watch-list, not write. The gating questions for a future check: does the team pick AEC and prove paying, retained customers off the Malaysian mandate (convert Petronas/TNBR/CLJ from logos to revenue), and can they show the localization head-start compounds into a real moat? Strong founder access via the accelerator makes them worth tracking into their first priced round, but the bar for a follow-on is not met at this stage."
