    "zh": "AppWorks Funds 的核心論點是 AI（首要）、Web3 與 B2B SaaS／marketplaces，並帶有明確的台灣＋東南亞（GSEA）地理任務與具防禦性的資料／IP／網路護城河。Krush 幾乎在每一根支柱上都不符：(1) 它是 B2C 消費者／社交約會——非 AppWorks 偏好的 B2B／marketplace 型態；(2) 其『AI』是已商品化的人臉驗證，而非 deep-tech 或資料護城河；(3) 它不是 Web3；(4) 最關鍵的是，其市場是美國／西方亞洲離散族群（紐約／洛杉磯／舊金山→加拿大／英國／澳洲），而非台灣或 ASEAN——因此對 AppWorks 至關重要的 GSEA 任務基本上未被滿足。身為 AW#32 加速器校友（免股權）建立了關係，但該公司並不符合 AppWorks Funds 會選擇性投入後續股權支票的條件。",
    "en": "AppWorks Funds' core thesis is AI (primary), Web3, and B2B SaaS/marketplaces with a hard Taiwan+Southeast Asia (GSEA) geographic mandate and defensible data/IP/network moats. Krush misses on nearly every pillar: (1) it is B2C consumer/social dating — not AppWorks' favored B2B/marketplace shape; (2) the 'AI' is commoditized face verification, not a deep-tech or data moat; (3) it is not Web3; (4) crucially, its market is the US/Western Asian diaspora (NY/LA/SF → Canada/UK/Australia), NOT Taiwan or ASEAN — so the GSEA mandate, which is central to AppWorks, is essentially unmet. Being an AW#32 accelerator alum (equity-free) creates a relationship, but the company does not match what AppWorks Funds selectively writes follow-on equity checks into."
