   "verdict": {
    "zh": "多方論點（BULL）：一個真實、已出貨的產品，搭配可查證、有能力的創始團隊（Amazon／Samsung／TuSimple／ProtoPie 背景）、一筆來自 Mashup Ventures 的真實機構種子投資、一個清晰的利基（亞洲離散族群有目的約會）並乘著滑動疲乏的順風，且早期 app store 口碑尚可（4.28★）。若自報的留存（每日訪客 10 倍；35% 5 天回訪；57% 次週宣稱）能經得起檢驗，那對約會領域而言會是異常強勁。空方論點（BEAR，主導）：這對 AppWorks Funds 的後續投資而言契合度很差。(a) 地理錯誤——它鎖定西方亞洲離散族群，而非 GSEA（台灣＋東南亞），削弱了 AppWorks 的核心任務。(b) 它是消費者約會，一個以留存薄弱、CAC 高、轉換成本低、護城河弱著稱的類別——落在 AppWorks 的 AI／Web3／B2B 焦點之外。(c) 主打的『前 Kakao』團隊宣稱未經驗證，且與 LinkedIn／媒體相左，是一個可信度警訊。(d) 牽引力規模小且模糊（累計下載 23k-75k；種子金額未揭露；無營收數據）。(e) 競爭場域擁擠，充滿資金更雄厚的玩家（EME Hive、Tantan、Coffee Meets Bagel、Match Group）。結論：AppWorks Funds 最有可能對後續投資支票選擇 PASS（放棄）。它仍可作為一位受重視的加速器社群校友，但市場錯位（非 GSEA）、論點錯位（消費者約會 vs. AI／Web3／B2B）、護城河薄弱，以及稀薄／未驗證的牽引力，使後續股權投資不太可能。我只會在團隊 (i) 展現出可信、經第三方驗證且遠高於約會業界水準的留存率，且 (ii) 展現出具體且有牽引力的台灣／東南亞擴張時，才重新考慮。",
    "en": "BULL CASE: A real, shipping product with an identifiable, competent founding team (Amazon/Samsung/TuSimple/ProtoPie pedigree), a genuine institutional seed from Mashup Ventures, a clear niche (Asian-diaspora intentional dating) riding a swipe-fatigue tailwind, and decent early app-store sentiment (4.28★). If the self-reported retention (10x daily visitors; 35% 5-day return; 57% next-week claim) holds up under scrutiny, that would be unusually strong for dating. BEAR CASE (dominant): This is a poor fit for an AppWorks Funds follow-on. (a) Geography is wrong — it targets the Western Asian diaspora, not GSEA (Taiwan+SEA), undercutting AppWorks' core mandate. (b) It's consumer dating, a category with notoriously weak retention, high CAC, low switching costs, and weak moats — outside AppWorks' AI/Web3/B2B focus. (c) The headline 'ex-Kakao' team claim is unverified and contradicted by LinkedIn/press, a credibility flag. (d) Traction is small and ambiguous (23k-75k cumulative downloads; undisclosed seed; no revenue data). (e) Competitive field is crowded with better-funded players (EME Hive, Tantan, Coffee Meets Bagel, Match Group). VERDICT: AppWorks Funds would most likely PASS on a follow-on check. It could remain a valued accelerator-community alum, but the market mismatch (non-GSEA), thesis mismatch (consumer dating vs. AI/Web3/B2B), weak moat, and thin/unverified traction make an equity follow-on unlikely. I'd only reconsider if the team (i) shows credible, third-party-verified retention well above dating norms, AND (ii) demonstrates a concrete Taiwan/SEA expansion with traction."
   }
